## Review Checklist
1. **Endpoint consistency**: every "endpoint" field must EXACTLY match one of the API Endpoints above. Fix any mismatch (e.g., endpoint says "GET /users" but steps call "POST /users/login"; unify to the real endpoint).
2. **CRUD completeness**: for every resource, ensure Create/Read/Update/Delete are all covered; add missing operations (e.g., missing PUT/PATCH update cases, update of non-existent user, unauthorized update, duplicate email conflict, password change).
3. **Assertability**: rewrite vague expectations into machine-checkable assertions (explicit status code + field value or field presence/absence, e.g., "Response body does NOT contain the password field").
4. **Boundary**: add min/max length tests, pagination limit maximum, field case-sensitivity, empty strings.
5. **Security**: add SQL injection / XSS, rate limiting (account-level and IP-level), token expiry / refresh, IDOR / horizontal authorization, password strength complexity.
6. **Performance**: add P95 response time baseline and concurrency/throughput tests.
7. **Tags**: fill the "tags" array with labels (smoke, regression, auth, crud, boundary, security, performance).
8. **Cleanup & idempotency**: add teardown/cleanup for created data and duplicate-submission cases so tests stay re-runnable.
9. **I18N**: add unicode / emoji / whitespace / special-character handling cases.

